    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0364" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/989½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">30 March, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This note<anchor n="71"
                        xml:id="d254-f1"/> is entirely satisfactory to me with the alterations you
                    have suggested, and I entirely approve of adding the paragraph you have drawn as
                    the concluding passage of the note.</p>
                <p>I hope that the encyphering and all the handling of this note will be under the
                    safeguards as to privacy which we agreed upon, so that there may be no garbled
                    versions of it current before it reaches London. I assume that it will be agreed
                    between Washington and London that it will be published here upon its receipt
                    and delivery there.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d254-f1" n="71" xml:id="d254-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the note as sent, see <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_152">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1915, supp., p.
                    152</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
